Hi,

I'm working on a nice Dartseq dataset encompassing seven penguin taxa. I have completed most of my key analyses now, and have gone back to tick off some of the more basic statistics (global Fst and Fis).

I notice that many researchers generate AMOVA based Fst using Genodive... and I also note that you can import a Structure file into Genodive. My structure file that I generate with DartR does not work in Genodive, yet it worked in Structure (even though I did have to remove the loci names). I was wondering if anyone else has had this issue with this conversion from DartR to Genodive, or if there is an alternative software that is recommended to generate these statistics?

The script I'm using to generate my Structure file is:

gl2structure(glpenguin, outfile=file.path("~/Documents/DartR/penguin.str"))

DartR works great for most other things I've needed it for - and it came at a perfect time for me to learn how to untangle and analyse SNPs (thank you!).

Tess

